{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490269,"nonce":"jTbh2qw00l92yDthcBB8Pu7SGTw=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABRbl5Vg","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/29","origin":"github"},"title":"Protect tutor credentials outside the webview","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nProvide the privileged credential boundary used by tutor providers. Store app-owned plaintext authentication data outside the webview with atomic updates, owner-only platform permissions, redacted status responses, and complete sign-out deletion.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Credential creation and replacement are atomic and recover safely from an interrupted write.\n- [ ] POSIX storage uses mode `0600`; Windows storage uses a verified equivalent owner-only ACL.\n- [ ] The webview can request provider status, authenticate, and sign out without receiving raw credential values.\n- [ ] Credentials never appear in browser storage, logs, errors, tutor context, sessions, or exported artifacts.\n- [ ] Sign-out deletes the selected provider credential and updates visible status.\n- [ ] An insecure existing credential file is repaired or rejected according to a documented policy.\n- [ ] Contract tests use synthetic credentials and inspect real temporary file permissions and redaction.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- git-bug issue `d2438d7` — Spike Pi providers and authentication in packaged Deno\n- git-bug issue `f264662` — Package the shared IDE in a desktop window","files":null}]}